WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:03.929
To finish, six setups built from everything in this course.

2
00:00:03.929 --> 00:00:05.954
None of them took more than a minute.

3
00:00:05.954 --> 00:00:06.830
Let's get weird.

4
00:00:07.285 --> 00:00:07.540
One.

5
00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:08.690
A feedback tunnel.

6
00:00:08.690 --> 00:00:14.761
The camera, amber phosphor, circular burn-in with a long decay, and the camera slowly orbiting.

7
00:00:21.075 --> 00:00:25.393
Every frame smears into the next, so the picture leaves a trail of itself.

8
00:00:25.844 --> 00:00:26.079
Two.

9
00:00:26.079 --> 00:00:27.197
Interleaved worlds.

10
00:00:27.197 --> 00:00:31.847
Dual Raster, alternate lines, with raster B pushed the opposite way and turned.

11
00:00:31.847 --> 00:00:34.555
Two copies of the same camera, woven together.

12
00:00:34.555 --> 00:00:42.384
One pushes toward you, the other falls away, and every other scan line flips between them, so the picture seems to argue with itself.

13
00:00:42.384 --> 00:00:45.209
Orbit around it, and the two layers slide apart.

14
00:00:51.837 --> 00:00:52.205
Three.

15
00:00:52.205 --> 00:00:59.516
Resonant chaos, loaded from a saved patch: filtered noise wobbling the rotation, and a feedback loop chasing the depth.

16
00:00:59.516 --> 00:01:01.728
Wireframe mode makes it a sculpture.

17
00:01:02.923 --> 00:01:03.237
Four.

18
00:01:03.237 --> 00:01:04.116
Sound terrain.

19
00:01:04.116 --> 00:01:10.020
The microphone drives spectrum displacement, so every frequency band lifts its own scan lines.

20
00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:11.653
Magenta, with heavy bloom.

21
00:01:22.292 --> 00:01:22.604
Five.

22
00:01:22.604 --> 00:01:24.478
The raster, turned inside out.

23
00:01:24.478 --> 00:01:31.101
One low frequency oscillator on horizontal linearity, another on vertical, and then we turn the amount up.

24
00:01:31.101 --> 00:01:36.223
The lines pinch, fold, and flip over themselves, and all of it is the same camera.

25
00:02:24.579 --> 00:02:24.846
Six.

26
00:02:24.846 --> 00:02:28.927
A Lissajous figure, in red and cyan anaglyph, drifting in 3D.

27
00:02:28.927 --> 00:02:30.198
Put on the glasses.

28
00:02:37.708 --> 00:02:39.080
That's the instrument.

29
00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:41.887
Now go make something nobody has seen before.
